  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reinforcing the National HIV and TB Response in Mozambique - Mozambique (01-Jan-2024-31-Dec-2026)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mozambique, TB/HIV, Centro de Colabora&#xe7;&#xe3;o em Sa&#xfa;de (CCS)This program has the following goals: Reduce new HIV infections 25% by 2025.  Reduce HIV-related deaths 30% by 2025.  Reduce the estimated percentage of child HIV infections from HIV-positive women delivering in the past 12 months to &lt;5% by 2025.  Reduce the incidence of TB (per 100,000 population) from 361 in 2022 to 310 in 2026.  Reduce TB-related Mortality (per 100,000 population) from 43 in 2022 to 35 in 2026. The objectives of this program are: Increase coverage of PLHIV on ART to 90% by 2025..  Increase viral supression among PLHIV to 86% by 2025..  Identify 90% of incident TB cases and offer appropriate treatment to all them.  Identfy 90% of incident TB cases in vulnerable population, offer appropriate treatment to all of them to successfully treat 90% of them.  Identify all incident cases of resistant tuberculosis offer appropriate treatment.  Successfully treat 90% or more of all drug-sensitive tuberculosis patients regardless of their HIV status</narrative>
  </description>
